      "refersTo": "pill",
      "description": "Line state: lamp dot plus label on a 12% tint.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-pill ds-pill-ok\"><span class=\"ds-dot\"></span>Working</span> <span class=\"ds-pill ds-pill-warn\"><span class=\"ds-dot\"></span>Registering</span> <span class=\"ds-pill ds-pill-orange\"><span class=\"ds-dot\"></span>Tunnel down</span> <span class=\"ds-pill ds-pill-danger\"><span class=\"ds-dot\"></span>PIN problem</span>",
      "css": ".ds-pill{font-family:\"Adwaita Sans\",ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:2px 9px;border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.6;white-space:nowrap;color:var(--p);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--p) 12%,transparent);border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--p) 28%,transparent);}.ds-dot{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--d);}.ds-pill-ok{--p:#15803d;--d:#16a34a;}.ds-pill-warn{--p:#a16207;--d:#eab308;}.ds-pill-orange{--p:#c2410c;--d:#f97316;}.ds-pill-danger{--p:#dc2626;--d:#ef4444;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Line Pipeline",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "",
      "description": "Five-step health bar on each reader card; shows where a line stopped.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-pipe\"><div><i class=\"done\"></i><span>SIM</span></div><div><i class=\"done\"></i><span>ePDG DNS</span></div><div><i class=\"cur\"></i><span>Tunnel</span></div><div><i></i><span>IMS reg</span></div><div><i></i><span>Working</span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-pipe{display:flex;gap:6px;width:420px;font-family:\"Adwaita Sans\",ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-pipe>div{flex:1;text-align:center;}.ds-pipe i{display:block;height:5px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--border-strong,#d4d4d8);}.ds-pipe i.done{background:#16a34a;}.ds-pipe i.cur{background:#ca8a04;}.ds-pipe span{display:block;font-size:10px;color:var(--text-mute,#a1a1aa);margin-top:4px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Reader Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card",
      "description": "One physical reader and its line: header, state pill, facts, ghost actions.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-card\"><div class=\"ds-card-head\"><strong>Reader 0 \u00b7 Alcor Link AK9563</strong><span class=\"ds-cpill\"><span></span>Working</span></div><div class=\"ds-card-sub\">O2 (DE)</div><dl class=\"ds-facts\"><dt>Carrier</dt><dd>262-03</dd><dt>SMSC</dt><dd class=\"m\">+49176000443</dd></dl></div>",
      "css": ".ds-card{font-family:\"Adwaita Sans\",ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;width:420px;padding:20px;background:var(--panel,#fff);border:1px solid var(--border,#e4e4e7);border-radius:10px;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(9,9,11,.04);color:var(--text,#09090b);}.ds-card-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:15px;}.ds-card-sub{font-size:12px;color:var(--text-mute,#a1a1aa);margin-top:2px;}.ds-cpill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:2px 9px;border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;color:#15803d;background:color-mix(in srgb,#15803d 12%,transparent);border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,#15803d 28%,transparent);}.ds-cpill span{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:999px;background:#16a34a;}.ds-facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:4px 12px;margin:14px 0 0;font-size:13px;}.ds-facts dt{color:var(--text-mute,#a1a1aa);}.ds-facts dd{margin:0;color:var(--text-soft,#3f3f46);}.ds-facts .m{font-family:\"Adwaita Mono\",ui-monospace,monospace;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Switchboard",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Switchboard\"**\n\nThe UI is an operator's panel of telephone lines. Each SIM is a line on the board, and the board's job is to say at a glance which lines are live, which are coming up, and which are down and where. The chrome stays quiet: zinc neutrals, hairline borders, one indigo accent, compact type. That way the status lamps (green, amber, orange, red, slate) are what the eye finds first.\n\nIt is dense the way a desk instrument is: 12\u201314px text, tight 6\u201312px gaps, real values printed in full (IMSI, SMSC, P-CSCF, codecs) rather than summarised. Light and dark are equal citizens; dark is a true near-black board (#09090b), not a grey inversion, and it drops card shadows entirely. On a phone the board turns into a bottom tab bar and single-pane views so the softphone and messages work one-handed.\n\nThe stylesheet's own label for this direction is \"clean devtool\"; the Switchboard is what that devtool is for.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Zinc neutral scale, one indigo accent, semantic state colours with fixed meanings",
      "Hairline 1px borders define surfaces; shadows are near-absent at rest",
      "Small, precise type in Adwaita Sans; Adwaita Mono with tabular figures for identifiers and live numbers",
      "Gently rounded (8\u201310px) rectangles, full pills for status",
      "Every theme token has a light and a dark value; both must be checked"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Lamp Rule",
        "body": "Green, amber, orange and red belong to line health. A pill, banner or dot in one of those colours always means a state, and a state always uses the same colour wherever it appears (dashboard pill, pipeline, softphone registration).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tint, Not Fill Rule",
        "body": "Status surfaces are tints mixed from the lamp token: pills at 12% background / 28% border, banners at 9% over the panel / 35% border. Solid fills are reserved for dots, pipeline bars and destructive buttons.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Steady Digits Rule",
        "body": "Anything that updates in place (timers, counters, signal values, `<time>`) uses tabular figures so it never jitters.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Float-Only Rule",
        "body": "Shadows mark things above the board: toasts, modals, sticky bars. Resting cards are drawn by their border.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** define every new colour as a CSS custom property with light, dark and auto-dark values in `index.css`, and check both themes.",
      "**Do** colour line health with the lamp tokens through `.pill-*`, `.banner-*` and `.st-*` classes, so a state looks the same everywhere.",
      "**Do** use ghost buttons for routine line actions and keep one primary button per group.",
      "**Do** print real identifiers in full, in Adwaita Mono with tabular figures where they update.",
      "**Do** use container queries for layouts inside the content area, because the sidebar takes width."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use green, amber, orange or red for anything that isn't a line or result state (The Lamp Rule).",
      "**Don't** put shadows on resting cards beyond the card-rest token; shadows are for toasts, modals and sticky bars.",
      "**Don't** hard-code hex values in component inline styles when a token exists; `#ca8a04` in the pipeline and the `.st-*` dots are the known exceptions.",
      "**Don't** add a second typeface; hierarchy comes from size and weight in Adwaita Sans."
    ]
  }
}
